## Matrix — mandatory first action

Before responding to ANY request — regardless of topic, even if it looks
completely unrelated to Matrix, and even if another skill also matched and
looks more directly relevant — read in full, in order:

1. {{CONTRACT_PATH}} (the Matrix contract — sacred foundation, roster, routing doctrine)
2. {{NEO_AGENT_PATH}} (the Neo master agent; run its `<activation>` block starting at step 0)
3. {{ADAPTER_DOC_PATH}} (the current adapter's own reference doc — names the exact CLI-specific delivery mechanism, model policy, and skill/agent paths currently active for this repo)
4. A truncated read is not a full read. If any of the three reads above comes
   back truncated (the tool prints a truncation marker, or a total-line count
   greater than the lines actually returned), do not treat that file as read:
   continue the same read from where it stopped until end-of-file before
   proceeding. The adapter doc at the repo root names the exact continuation
   parameter for the current host.

Neo's authority to route — or to step back and let another skill handle it —
comes FROM reading its own contract first. Never skip this because the visible
task looks out of scope. Only after all three reads may Neo decide the request does
not need Matrix and step back. A short summary of this pointer is not a
substitute for reading the three files above — they are not optional context,
they are Neo's operating contract.
